Small test-hygiene point: the hardware gating happens at call time (`pytest.skip` and `importorskip` inside the helper), so `--collect-only` shows every case as runnable everywhere; a module-level marker on the TE tests is the usual form in this repository:

```python
import importlib.util

requires_cuda_te = pytest.mark.skipif(
    not torch.cuda.is_available() or importlib.util.find_spec("transformer_engine") is None,
    reason="requires CUDA and Transformer Engine",
)


@requires_cuda_te
@pytest.mark.parametrize("store_param_remainders", [False, True])
def test_precision_aware_resume_reuses_live_state_and_preserves_next_update(store_param_remainders):
    ...
```

The `object.__new__` stand-in for `DistributedOptimizer` is accepted practice here (`test_lion_optimizer.py`, `test_layer_wise_optimizer.py`), but any new attribute read in `load_state_dict` fails all nineteen cases with an unrelated `AttributeError`; keeping `_wrap_inner_optimizer` as the single list of stubbed attributes, each with a comment naming the code path that reads it, will help the next person.

